WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.852
Sally plugs the cable
in by the whiteboard.

2
00:00:07.852 --> 00:00:12.000
The Core wakes and opens
its own Wi-Fi network.

3
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:18.700
John joins the Core's own network from
his phone, then picks the home network.

4
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.385
Sally messages the agent
she named Juniper.

5
00:00:22.385 --> 00:00:27.070
The reply comes from the Core,
a floor above her craft room.

6
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.750
<v Juniper>Hello, Sally. I am Juniper.
What should we start with?

7
00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.521
A sleeve wipes Thursday
off the whiteboard.

8
00:00:35.521 --> 00:00:41.250
Its twin in Yuvomi on the Core still
has the dentist and the dinner.

9
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.054
Jean measures her shared room
for a maths scale drawing.

10
00:00:46.054 --> 00:00:52.400
draw.io opens from the Core, and she
draws the beds, the desk and the shelf.

11
00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.017
Juniper drafts a renewal
reply from last spring's

12
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:59.145
thread, which Sally connected
to Companion Memory.

13
00:00:59.145 --> 00:01:02.750
Sally checks the figures,
then sends it herself.

14
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.848
John's last push today, a
branch called shelf-jig,

15
00:01:06.848 --> 00:01:11.900
lands in Gitea on the Core, issues
and pull requests beside it.

16
00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:17.137
Steve's game runs on the Core,
beside the kitchen whiteboard.

17
00:01:17.137 --> 00:01:22.650
He signs in with his own Valve
account, and the den TV shows it.

18
00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:29.800
A craft room, a workbench, a den and a
shared bedroom, on one Companion Core.

19
00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.409
Your family's week, notes and homework
can live on a Companion Core.

20
00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:39.340
Browse the Companion Hub store
and pick your first apps.

21
00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.250
UnCloud your life.
